📋 LIVE DEPLOYMENT — SHORT SHEET
Which file to edit?
Only .env on your live server. Nothing else. No code, no migration changes — just the env file. (Migrations need running once with php artisan migrate --force, but that's not "editing a file".)

Your 3 scenarios — .env values
Scenario 1 — ONE branch, ONE set of APIs

LEAD_SYNC_BRANCH_ID=2

INDIAMART_AGROTECH_KEY=<key from IndiaMart portal>
INDIAMART_PURVEE_KEY=
INDIAMART_VORTEX_KEY=
Only branch 2 sees the Sync button. Pulls from Agrotech account.

Scenario 2 — ANOTHER branch with ITS OWN APIs
⚠️ Current design supports ONE set of keys per deployment — all enabled branches share them.

If you literally need branch 1 → Agrotech account and branch 2 → some different IndiaMart account, the keys can't be split today. Tell me and I'll add per-branch overrides (10-line change). Until then, treat all branches as sharing the same 3 IndiaMart accounts (which is your real-world setup — Inorbvict has 3 accounts, not 3 branches × different accounts).

Scenario 3 — 3-4 branches sharing the SAME APIs ✅ (current design)

LEAD_SYNC_BRANCH_ID=1,2,3,4

INDIAMART_AGROTECH_KEY=<key>
INDIAMART_PURVEE_KEY=<key>
INDIAMART_VORTEX_KEY=<key>
Any user in branch 1, 2, 3, or 4 sees Sync. All four branches pull from the same 3 IndiaMart accounts. Leads land in each user's own tenant scope.

Commands after editing .env

php artisan migrate --force      # first deploy only — creates leads table
php artisan config:clear
npm run build                    # only if frontend changed
That's it.

How the real API actually works (short)

[User clicks Sync from IndiaMart]
   │
   ▼  POST /sales/leads/sync
[Cross_Border_Command server]
   │  Checks: is your branch_id in LEAD_SYNC_BRANCH_ID?
   │  If NO → 403, nothing happens.
   │  If YES → for each INDIAMART_*_KEY in .env:
   │
   ▼  GET https://mapi.indiamart.com/wservce/crm/crmListing/v2/
       ?glusr_crm_key=<KEY>
       &start_time=<7 days ago>
       &end_time=<today>
   │
[IndiaMart server]
   │  Returns JSON: { CODE: 200, RESPONSE: [...leads...] }
   │  OR: { CODE: 401, MESSAGE: "key expired" }
   │  OR: { CODE: 429, MESSAGE: "wait 5 min" }
   │
   ▼
[Cross_Border_Command server]
   │  For each lead in RESPONSE:
   │  - if country NOT in 190-country export list → mark disqualified
   │  - upsert into `leads` table by (client_id, platform, unique_query_id)
   │
   ▼  JSON back to browser
   │  { fetched: 12, created: 8, updated: 4, disqualified: 2, errors: [] }
   │
[Toast in UI]   "8 new · 4 updated · 2 disqualified"
[Table refreshes — new rows visible]
Real-world constraints
1 IndiaMart call per 5 minutes per key. Don't spam Sync.
7-day default window. Each sync grabs leads from the last 7 days.
Same lead synced twice = updated, not duplicated. Safe to re-run.
India sender = auto-disqualified (export-only CRM).
Expired keys return CODE 401 in the body — error surfaces as a toast.
Bottom line
Live deployment = edit 4 lines in .env + run 3 commands.
Nothing else changes. No code edits, no per-branch keys (unless you ask), no DB seeders.

Tell me if you want per-branch different keys (Scenario 2 done properly) — I'll add it.